<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Architecture Overview

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
High Level System Architecture

.. image:: _images/sds_arch_1.png

Main Modules

The design of the application is based on the MVVM pattern. There are three core components in the MVVM pattern: the model, the view, and the view model. Each serves a distinct purpose. The diagram below shows the relationships between the three components.

.. image:: _images/sds_arch_2.png

The MVVN design pattern is implemented in the application as follows: the 4 th  layer is the gRPC wrapper for communication with the Record and Verify services.

.. image:: _images/sds_arch_3.png
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: SW-H10TG-
TITLE: Design Items

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-269
TITLE: A visual indication for system faults
STATEMENT: >>>
The GCB data store maintains an immutable list of the currently latched fault records and
publishes a fault-changed event whenever the list changes. The fault view renders each
record's category, formatted message, captured control-board state, and captured runtime.
General fault-category flags continue to drive the system-fault indication.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-284
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-255
TITLE: Beam On process
STATEMENT: >>>
The flow Beaming On (delivering emission) process should be implemented as described in the following chart diagram:

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   graph TD
       A(["Plan loaded for treatment"]) --> B{"Plan can be executed"}
       
       B -- Yes --> C{"State = Startup / Cold / Primed"}
       B -- No ----> ShowError["Show plan error message"]
       
       C -- Yes --> Prepare["Left button: Prepare"]
       C -- No --> CheckStaged{"State = Staged"}
       
       CheckStaged -- Yes ----> CentralResume["Central button: Resume"]
       CheckStaged -- No ----> ShowError
       
       Prepare --> PressPrepare[/press Prepare/]
       PressPrepare --> StatePrimed{"State = Primed"}
       
       StatePrimed -- Yes --> LoadStage["Load and stage plan"]
       StatePrimed -- No --> WarmUp["WarmUp"] --> LoadStage
       
       LoadStage --> ConfirmRelease["Confirm and release plan"]
       ConfirmRelease --> HVSetup["HVPSCheck and HVSetup"]
       HVSetup --> StateReady["State = Ready<br>Central button: BeamOn"]
       
       StateReady --> PressBeamOn[/press BeamOn/]
       PressBeamOn --> StartEmission["Start emission"]
       
       StartEmission --> CheckInterrupt{"Fault or user interrupt"}
       
       CheckInterrupt -- No --> EmissionComplete["Emission complete"]
       EmissionComplete --> ResetTimers["Central button: ResetTimers"]
       ResetTimers --> EndNode([end])
       
       CheckInterrupt -- Yes --> CheckFault{"Fault state"}
       
       CheckFault -- Yes --> ClearErrors["Central button: ClearErrors"]
       ClearErrors --> PressClear[/press ClearErrors/]
       PressClear --> CentralResume
       
       CheckFault -- No --> CentralResume
       
       CentralResume --> PressResume[/press Resume/]
       PressResume --> ConfirmRelease
       
       ShowError --> EndNode
   </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-9
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-43
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-73
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-271
TITLE: Clear Fault Flags
STATEMENT: >>>
The fault view sends the clear command through the main-board model and unified GCB command
interface. The firmware acknowledges the command, clears its latched records, increments
the clear epoch, and publishes an empty fault update. The telemetry processor applies that
update to the GCB data store, which notifies the fault view.

.. raw:: html

    <pre class="mermaid">
    sequenceDiagram
        participant FaultsViewModel
        participant MainBoardModel
        participant GcbCommandInterface
        participant Firmware
        participant SystemTelemetryProcessor
        participant GCBDataStore

        FaultsViewModel->>MainBoardModel: ClearFaults
        MainBoardModel->>GcbCommandInterface: ClearFaults
        GcbCommandInterface->>Firmware: [UDP] clear-fault directive
        Firmware-->>GcbCommandInterface: [UDP] command response
        Firmware-->>SystemTelemetryProcessor: [UDP] empty fault update, new clear epoch
        SystemTelemetryProcessor->>GCBDataStore: ApplyFaultUpdate
        GCBDataStore-->>FaultsViewModel: FaultsChangedEvent(empty)
    </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-284
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-249
TITLE: Confirmation of Treatment Plan
STATEMENT: >>>
.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
       autonumber
       
       box Application
           participant MainBoardModel
       end
       box ControlBoard
           participant Firmware
       end

       Note over MainBoardModel, Firmware: Board is in Staged state
       
       activate MainBoardModel
       loop "for each operational point"
           MainBoardModel->>Firmware: "[UDP] send operational parameters confirmation"
           activate Firmware
           Firmware-->>MainBoardModel: "[UDP] status response"
           deactivate Firmware
       end

       MainBoardModel->>Firmware: "[UDP] ReleasePlan command"
       activate Firmware
       Firmware-->>MainBoardModel: "[UDP] status response"
       deactivate Firmware

       Note over MainBoardModel: wait for Ready board state
       MainBoardModel->>MainBoardModel: 
       deactivate MainBoardModel
   </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-35
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-264
TITLE: Daily Warmup Process
STATEMENT: >>>
The flow for performing Daily Warmup should be implemented as described in the following sequence diagram:

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
       autonumber
       
       box Application
           participant DailyWarmUpViewModel
           participant MainBoardModel
           participant WarmupModel
       end
       box ControlBoard
           participant Firmware
       end
       box Record & Verify
           participant WarmupService
       end

       Note over DailyWarmUpViewModel, WarmupService: User initiates Warmup/Conditioning
       
       DailyWarmUpViewModel->>MainBoardModel: WarmUp
       activate DailyWarmUpViewModel
       activate MainBoardModel
       
       Note over MainBoardModel: check target filament current range
       MainBoardModel->>MainBoardModel: 

       alt "[Startup board state]"
           MainBoardModel->>Firmware: "[UDP] initialization command"
           activate Firmware
           Note over Firmware: initialize
           Firmware->>Firmware: 
           Firmware-->>MainBoardModel: "[UDP] status response"
           deactivate Firmware
           
           Note over MainBoardModel: wait for Cold state in the telemetry
           MainBoardModel->>MainBoardModel: 
       end

       MainBoardModel->>Firmware: "[UDP] Warmup/Conditioning command"
       activate Firmware
       Note over Firmware: start warming up
       Firmware->>Firmware: 
       Firmware-->>MainBoardModel: "[UDP] status response"
       deactivate Firmware

       Note over MainBoardModel: wait for Warmup/Conditioning terminal state
       MainBoardModel->>MainBoardModel: 

       MainBoardModel-->>DailyWarmUpViewModel: 
       deactivate MainBoardModel
       
       DailyWarmUpViewModel->>WarmupModel: Save Warmup/Conditioning event
       activate WarmupModel
       
       WarmupModel->>WarmupService: grpc: Save Warmup event
       activate WarmupService
       Note over WarmupService: create a DB record
       WarmupService->>WarmupService: 
       WarmupService-->>WarmupModel: stored record
       deactivate WarmupService
       
       Note over WarmupModel: add record to the list
       WarmupModel->>WarmupModel: 
       WarmupModel-->>DailyWarmUpViewModel: 
       deactivate WarmupModel
       deactivate DailyWarmUpViewModel
   </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-1
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-265
TITLE: Display System Telemetry
STATEMENT: >>>
The receive-only telemetry service listens for unsolicited GCB datagrams. Device-information
packets identify the firmware version and mode; the system telemetry processor selects the
matching normal or calibration parser. Unsupported versions and malformed packets are
rejected without replacing the last valid state.

Valid telemetry is converted to an immutable semantic snapshot. Firmware-specific fields
are represented as unavailable when absent. Snapshots are published at most every 250 ms,
while device information continues to refresh the selected parser. If no valid telemetry
is received for 1.5 seconds, the processor publishes an unavailable snapshot.

.. raw:: html

    <pre class="mermaid">
    sequenceDiagram
        participant TelemetryView
        participant GCBDataStore
        participant MainBoardModel
        participant SystemTelemetryProcessor
        participant TelemetryService
        participant Firmware

        Firmware->>TelemetryService: [UDP] device information, 1 Hz
        TelemetryService->>SystemTelemetryProcessor: Select parser by version and mode
        Firmware->>TelemetryService: [UDP] system telemetry, 100 Hz
        TelemetryService->>SystemTelemetryProcessor: Process datagram
        SystemTelemetryProcessor->>MainBoardModel: OnSystemTelemetryChanged(ISystemTelemetry?)
        MainBoardModel->>GCBDataStore: Set immutable SystemTelemetry
        GCBDataStore-->>TelemetryView: Publish semantic telemetry
    </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-2
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-82
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-6
TITLE: EMR: Treatment Console - Load For Treatment Plan Flow
STATEMENT: >>>
The treatment console application shall be triggered by the base (internal) application with a treatment plan to be delivered. When the application is triggered, the patient details, plan details, and treatment fields should be displayed, and the plan should be ready for activation.

The following sequence diagram describes the workflow of LoadForTreatment flow (should be moved to detailed design)

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
       autonumber
       actor User
       participant CC
       participant Moses
       participant DB
       participant TC

       User->>CC: LoadForTreatment
       activate CC
       CC->>Moses: LoadForTreatment
       activate Moses
       Moses->>DB: UpdatePlanTreatmentState(Pending)
       activate DB
       DB->>TC: LoadForTreatment Event
       activate TC
       TC->>Moses: UpdatePlanTreatmentState(Loaded)
       Moses->>DB: UpdatePlanTreatmentState(Loaded)
       DB->>CC: PlanLoaded Event
       activate CC
       deactivate CC
       deactivate TC
       deactivate DB
       deactivate Moses
       deactivate CC
   </pre>

1. The user presses the LoadForTreatment buttoning the Base UI.
2. C&C sends LoadForTreatment API to Moses.
3. Moses (DB Service) fetches all Pending plans from DB.

4. If there are no Pending plans, Moses changes the plan state to Pending
5. Moses triggers LoadForTreatment Event with patient details, plan, and treatment fields
6. Treatment Console (external) receives the event and loads the plan into the UI.
7. Treatment Console sends TreatmentLoaded API
8. Treatment Console locks the treatment view.
9. Moses changes the plan state to Loaded
10. Moses trigger the TreatmentLoaded event to the C&C
11. C&C locks the plan view.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-32
  ROLE: Refines

