[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-278
TITLE: Play sound during emission
STATEMENT: >>>
The flow for providing audible indication during active emission should be implemented as described in the following sequence diagram:

.. raw:: html

    <pre class="mermaid">
    sequenceDiagram
        box Application
            participant MainView
            participant Converter as GcbStatusToRadiation<br/>HazardActiveStateConverter
            participant GCBDataStore
        end
        box Control Board
            participant Firmware
        end

        [?] ->> MainView: OnLoad
        activate MainView
        
        MainView->>GCBDataStore: getSystemTelemetry
        activate GCBDataStore
        
        activate Firmware
        Firmware-->>GCBDataStore: OnTelemetryChanged
        deactivate Firmware
        
        GCBDataStore-->>MainView: return SystemTelemetry
        deactivate GCBDataStore

        MainView->>Converter: convert
        activate Converter
        Converter->>Converter: if emission return else return false
        activate Converter
        deactivate Converter
        Converter->>MainView: return state
        deactivate Converter

        MainView->>MainView: ChangeRadiationIconColor(state)
        activate MainView
        deactivate MainView
        
        MainView->>MainView: PlaySound(state)
        activate MainView
        deactivate MainView
        
        deactivate MainView
    </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-87
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-262
TITLE: Prevent Treatment if the Daily Safety checks is not completed
STATEMENT: >>>
The flow for Prevent Treatment when no daily safety checks are performed should be implemented as described in the following flow chart diagram:

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   graph TD
       A(["Ready for Prepare"]) --> B[/press Prepare/]
       B --> C{"Daily SafetyCheck is done?"}
       
       C -- Yes --> D{"Is it complete?"}
       C -- No ----> ShowError["Show error, block treatment"]
       
       D -- Yes ----> ProceedPrepare["Proceed with Prepare"]
       D -- No --> E{"Door interlock, e-stop,<br>normal stop checks passed?"}
       
       E -- Yes --> Alert[/Safety alert:<br>ask for confirmation/]
       E -- No --> ShowError
       
       Alert --> F{"Proceed treatment?"}
       
       F -- Yes --> ProceedPrepare
       F -- No ----> EndNode([end])
       
       ProceedPrepare --> EndNode
       ShowError --> EndNode
   </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-96
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-97
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-250
TITLE: Prevent treatment plan execution if an interlock is active
STATEMENT: >>>
.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
       autonumber

       box Application
           participant OperatePlanViewModelBase
           participant InterlockIndicators
           participant BeamOnCommand
           participant GCBDataStore
           participant SystemTelemetryProcessor
           participant TelemetryService
       end
       box ControlBoard
           participant Firmware
       end

       Firmware-->>TelemetryService: [UDP] unsolicited telemetry
       TelemetryService->>SystemTelemetryProcessor: Process datagram
       SystemTelemetryProcessor->>GCBDataStore: Set semantic snapshot
       GCBDataStore-->>OperatePlanViewModelBase: SystemTelemetryChanged

       activate OperatePlanViewModelBase
       Note over OperatePlanViewModelBase: Check semantic interlocks and active fault categories
       alt Interlock or fault is active
           OperatePlanViewModelBase->>BeamOnCommand: disable
       end
       deactivate OperatePlanViewModelBase

       GCBDataStore-->>InterlockIndicators: SystemTelemetryChanged
       InterlockIndicators->>InterlockIndicators: Render ready, active, or unavailable
   </pre>
