[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-270
TITLE: Retrieve Fault Information from Firmware
STATEMENT: >>>
The command interface retrieves a coherent snapshot of the latched fault list using indexed
requests. Each 45-word response is validated for packet shape, index, count, clear epoch,
fault category, printable NUL-terminated format string, format checksum, and argument count.
The interface retries the snapshot up to three times if the clear epoch changes during
retrieval. The main-board model replaces the GCB data store's active list only after a
coherent snapshot has been assembled.

.. raw:: html

    <pre class="mermaid">
    sequenceDiagram
        participant FaultsViewModel
        participant MainBoardModel
        participant GcbCommandInterface
        participant FaultEntryParser
        participant Firmware
        participant GCBDataStore

        FaultsViewModel->>MainBoardModel: GetFaults
        MainBoardModel->>GcbCommandInterface: GetFaults
        loop Entry index 0 through active count - 1
            GcbCommandInterface->>Firmware: [UDP] FaultInfoRequest(index)
            Firmware-->>GcbCommandInterface: [UDP] FaultInfoResponse(45 words)
            GcbCommandInterface->>FaultEntryParser: Validate and format entry
        end
        GcbCommandInterface-->>MainBoardModel: FaultSnapshot(epoch, entries)
        MainBoardModel->>GCBDataStore: ReplaceFaults
        GCBDataStore-->>FaultsViewModel: FaultsChangedEvent
    </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-284
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-261
TITLE: Retrieve Quality Checks Reports
STATEMENT: >>>
The flow for retrieving Quality Checks Report should be implemented as described in the following sequence diagram:

.. raw:: html

    <pre class="mermaid">
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        actor User
        box Application
            participant VM as QualityCheckReportsViewModel
            participant M as QcModel
        end
        box Record & Verify
            participant S as QC Services
        end

        VM->>VM: build list of QC configurations
        
        User->>VM: select collimator type and energy
        VM->>VM: find matching collimator configuration
        
        VM->>M: read configuration QC samples
        M->>S: grpc: read QC samples
        S-->>M: grpc: stored samples
        M-->>VM: list of samples
        VM-->>User: [Show list of samples]

        User->>VM: select a sample
        VM->>M: fetch sample data
        M->>S: read sample fields/intensities
        S-->>M: grpc: stored records
        M-->>VM: sample data

        VM->>M: fetch reference sample data
        M->>M: check for cached data
        
        alt No cached sample data
            M->>S: read sample fields/intensities
            S-->>M: grpc: stored records
            M->>M: cache as reference
        end
        
        M-->>VM: reference sample data
        
        VM->>VM: calc sample deviation from reference
        VM->>VM: update sample report view
        VM-->>User: [Display updated report]

        User->>VM: switch raw/deviation report mode
    </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-93
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-94
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-274
TITLE: Retrieve treated patient details
STATEMENT: >>>
When the application is loaded, it searches for a plan that is pending to be loaded. Then, the plan details and all the patients' clinical data are initialized.

.. raw:: html

    <pre class="mermaid">
    sequenceDiagram
        participant Object as :Object
        participant OutdoorViewModel
        participant PlanModel
        participant TreatmentFieldCommands
        participant PrescriptionCommands
        participant TreatmentCommands

        [?] ->> Object: dispatch
        activate Object
        Object->>OutdoorViewModel: LookForPlanAsync
        activate OutdoorViewModel
        
        OutdoorViewModel->>PlanModel: LookPendingPlan
        activate PlanModel
        OutdoorViewModel->>Object: callback
        activate Object
        Object-->>OutdoorViewModel: return
        deactivate Object
        
        OutdoorViewModel->>PlanModel: SetPlan
        OutdoorViewModel-->>Object: return
        deactivate OutdoorViewModel
        
        PlanModel->>TreatmentFieldCommands: ReadFieldsAsync
        activate TreatmentFieldCommands
        deactivate TreatmentFieldCommands
        
        PlanModel->>PrescriptionCommands: ReadAsync
        activate PrescriptionCommands
        deactivate PrescriptionCommands
        
        PlanModel->>TreatmentCommands: Text
        activate TreatmentCommands
        deactivate TreatmentCommands
        
        deactivate PlanModel
        deactivate Object
    </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-85
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-273
TITLE: Show message for DB communication error
STATEMENT: >>>
The application will show a DB Communication error when the gRPC command throws a timeout exception. The exception will be populated through the MVVM model.

.. raw:: html

    <pre class="mermaid">
    sequenceDiagram
        box Application
            participant View
            participant ViewModel
            participant Model
            participant gRPCCommand
        end
        box Record & Verify
            participant Object as :Object
        end

        activate View
        View->>ViewModel: call
        activate ViewModel
        ViewModel->>Model: call
        activate Model
        Model->>gRPCCommand: call
        activate gRPCCommand
        gRPCCommand->>Object: call
        activate Object
        
        Object-->>gRPCCommand: GRPC_STATUS_DEADLINE_EXCEEDED
        deactivate Object
        
        gRPCCommand-->>Model: throw ex
        deactivate gRPCCommand
        Model-->>ViewModel: throw ex
        deactivate Model
        ViewModel-->>View: throw ex
        deactivate ViewModel
        
        View->>View: Show DB Communication Error message
        deactivate View
    </pre>
<<<

